### =====================================================================
### User/Profile API — core-monolith
### Team Rocket — Joshua Larez
### Base: http://localhost:8080
### Security: disabled in dev mode (no JWT required for now)
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@userId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### ACTUATOR — sanity check
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1. Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health
Accept: application/json

###

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### USER PROFILE — GET
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 2. Get profile by userId (profile must exist first — create via RabbitMQ event or POST below)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/profile
Accept: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-get-profile-001

###

### 3. Get notification preferences for a user
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/notification-prefs
Accept: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-get-prefs-001

###

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### USER PROFILE — UPDATE
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 4. Update profile — display name and bio
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-update-profile-001

{
  "displayName": "Joshua Larez",
  "bio": "Software engineer at Team Rocket. Working on Event Planner."
}

###

### 5. Update profile — with preferences (language, timezone, notification channel)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-update-profile-002

{
  "displayName": "Joshua Larez",
  "bio": "Updated bio with preferences.",
  "preferences": {
    "language": "nl",
    "timezone": "Europe/Amsterdam",
    "notificationChannel": "EMAIL"
  }
}

###

### 6. Update profile — push notifications, English
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-update-profile-003

{
  "displayName": "Joshua L.",
  "bio": "Short bio.",
  "preferences": {
    "language": "en",
    "timezone": "UTC",
    "notificationChannel": "PUSH"
  }
}

###

### 7. Update profile — IN_APP channel
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-update-profile-004

{
  "displayName": "Joshua Larez",
  "bio": "In-app notifications preferred.",
  "preferences": {
    "language": "nl",
    "timezone": "Europe/Amsterdam",
    "notificationChannel": "IN_APP"
  }
}

###

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### AVATAR — upload / remove
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 8. Upload avatar (multipart — pick a small jpg/png file on your machine)
# Change the file path to a real image on your system
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/avatar
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="avatar.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< C:/Users/ydcla/Pictures/avatar.jpg
--boundary--

###

### 9. Remove avatar
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/avatar
X-Correlation-Id: test-remove-avatar-001

###

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### VALIDATION — expected errors (4xx responses)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 10. Update profile — displayName too short (< 2 chars) → expect 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-validation-001

{
  "displayName": "J",
  "bio": "Valid bio"
}

###

### 11. Update profile — displayName too long (> 64 chars) → expect 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-validation-002

{
  "displayName": "ThisNameIsWayTooLongAndShouldFailValidationBecauseItExceedsSixtyFourCharacters",
  "bio": "Valid bio"
}

###

### 12. Update profile — bio too long (> 500 chars) → expect 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-validation-003

{
  "displayName": "Joshua Larez",
  "bio": ""
}

###

### 13. Update profile — invalid notification channel → expect 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-validation-004

{
  "displayName": "Joshua Larez",
  "bio": "Valid bio",
  "preferences": {
    "language": "nl",
    "timezone": "Europe/Amsterdam",
    "notificationChannel": "TELEGRAM"
  }
}

###

### 14. Get profile — non-existent userId → expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999/profile
Accept: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-not-found-001

###

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### SIMULATE AccountRegistered event (trigger profile auto-creation)
### In production this comes from Identity via RabbitMQ.
### For manual testing you can POST directly if a test endpoint exists,
### or publish the event via RabbitMQ management UI at:
###   http://localhost:15672  (login: ep / ep)
###   Exchange: ep.events
###   Routing key: identity.account.registered.v1
###   Body (JSON):
###   {
###     "accountId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
###     "email": "joshua@teamrocket.nl",
###     "occurredAt": "2026-06-03T09:00:00Z"
###   }
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
